From 87b1e0cbbe2cc31ab29e57595de98a72968fa31c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:49:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Desktop: test a mid-transfer upload stall; pin
 fetchJson's body-size deadline by behaviour, not a main.ts regex

Follow-ups from the PR #1966 review (pullrequestreview-5887725393):

1. New test: the server takes one chunk of a 32 MiB multipart upload and stops
   reading (socket backpressure, no response). The idle timer rejects it at the
   caller's 150 ms timeout, not the ~268 s body-scaled total budget, and the
   server provably received only part of the body. RED with the idle timer at
   the budget or removed.

2. fetchJson / fetchPublicJson now put the request on the wire through
   api-transport's sendWithRequestDeadline(deadline, open, {body, onError,
   requestState}): it takes the already-started deadline (so it started before
   http.request), opens the request, arms the deadline with the byte size of the
   same body it writes, marks requestState.bodySent, writes and ends. The
   regex over main.ts source in remote-down-gate.test.ts ("main.ts wiring",
   a banned test shape) is deleted; behavioural tests drive the helper with a
   fake request (order open -> arm -> end, armed with 20 bytes for a
   10-character UTF-8 body, bodySent set) and end to end against a live server
   (a body gets its upload allowance, the same wait without one times out). The
   existing deadline tests now go through the same helper. RED with arm()
   missing the body, using the character length, or not setting bodySent.
